WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.370
<v Instructor>So here's one more storage class,</v>

2
00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.810
but I wanted to make a separate lecture for it

3
00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.880
because it's a bit different than the other ones.

4
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.270
So the S3 Express One Zone storage class

5
00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.800
is high performance,

6
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.950
but for a single availability zone type of storage class.

7
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:14.820
What does that mean?

8
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.860
That means that your objects are stored

9
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.590
not on the standard bucket on S3,

10
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:22.350
but in what's called a directory bucket,

11
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.750
and it's a special type of S3 bucket.

12
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.030
But this bucket, instead of being distributed

13
00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.400
across multiple availability zone,

14
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.160
it's going to be in a single availability zone only,

15
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.160
and you get to choose which one you want it to be in.

16
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.660
So it's a different kind of bucket,

17
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.880
and that's why there is a different kind

18
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.830
as well of storage class.

19
00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.380
So it's a very specific use case, but the idea is that

20
00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.780
because you are in a single AZ,

21
00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.340
then you're going to be able to handle

22
00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.200
hundreds of thousands of requests per second

23
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.600
with single digit millisecond latency,

24
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.160
so very high performance.

25
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:57.000
You get about 10 times the performance of S3 standard

26
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.670
with about 50% lower the cost.

27
00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:04.200
So good durability, but the availability is of course lower

28
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.630
because now instead of being three availability zones

29
00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:09.570
with some replication, you only have one availability zone.

30
00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:12.570
And of course, if there is a problem on this AZ,

31
00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.910
you're going to be directly affected.

32
00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:18.300
So the idea of using S3 Express One Zone is

33
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.120
that you're gonna be able to co-locate your storage

34
00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.150
and compute resources in the same availability zone

35
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.470
and therefore reduce latency

36
00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.900
and maybe even reduce your networking cost.

37
00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.810
So the use cases are for latency sensitive apps,

38
00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:34.140
for data intensive apps, for AI and ML training,

39
00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.670
financial modeling, media processing,

40
00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:37.380
and high performance computing,

41
00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.240
and it's best integrated with, for example,

42
00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.900
with SageMaker Model Training, Athena, EMR, Glue,

43
00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:45.270
all these kind of data services.

44
00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.650
All right, so that's it for this lecture.

45
00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:49.653
I hope you liked it, and I will see you in the next lecture.

